{% block summary %}
<p>The OSLO Mobility – Timetable and Planning: Vehicle Planning application profile describes how the terms from the corresponding vocabulary should be used to describe how a public transport company uses its vehicles to provide the service.</p>
<p>The standard is based on <a href="https://netex-cen.eu/">NETEX.</a></p>
<p>Central class is Blok. A Block is a collection of consecutive Trips that are completed with the same vehicle from the moment it leaves the Garage until the moment it returns there. Blocks form the basis for the efficient deployment of vehicles and drivers, e.g. by spatially gluing together Trips of different lines.</p>
<p>Blocks include both Service Trips (on which passengers can get on or off, see OSLO Mobility – Timetable and Planning: Time Tables for more info) and Unloaded Trips.</p>
<p>Because Trips are linked to Day Types (weekdays, school holidays, etc.), this is also the case for the Blocks to which they belong and by linking the Day Types to actual dates, a Service Calendar can be drawn up.</p>
<p>Furthermore, Blocks are described by the Parking Points (depots) where the first Trip departs and the last one arrives. These can be further specialized to Garage Point and linked to physical Garages and service rooms (class Crew Base).</p>
<p>The Vehicle type with which the trips of the Block are carried out can also be specified, including information about the available passenger capacity.</p>
<p>Because in addition to Service Trips, Unloaded Trips can also be described, we also have Unloaded Trip Patterns in addition to Service Trip Patterns. More information about the Routes of these Trips and associated Lines follows from the association with the class Route. Furthermore, for each Trip, it is possible to specify which Points are visited along the way with the corresponding Arrival Times (for a further description of this, see also OSLO Mobility – Timetable and Planning: Time Tables).</p>
<p>Currently not in this standard is the linking of actual Vehicles and of Drivers to Blocks. Also out of scope at the moment are Driving times.</p>
